  "dct_description_sm": [
    "Coordinates approximate and based on Greenwich meridian",
    "Relief shown by hachures",
    "Bar scales in lower left: \"50 Geographische Meilen 15 auf 1*\", \"Aegyptisch Schönus 18 9/10 auf 1*\"",
    "From Library of Congress: Shows Egypt (before Sudan Campaign 1821), Greater or Ottoman Syria (circled by a line refering to Aenaze Beduin Tribe), Akka and Tarablus as administrative units (Ottoman Eyalat), may suggest the map was drawn about the time of the Turco-Egyptian Conflict over control of Arab Greater Syria, which developed to the Egyptian-Ottoman War, 1831-1833, or after",
    "In lower right: \"H. Leutemann sc.\""
